==============================================================================
[4] M0 = Var(O) = C(0) = nu([0,inf))  (identity, any centered O, positive KL measure)
==============================================================================
 C(0) = int e^{-sqrt(s)*0} dnu(s) = nu([0,inf)) = <O^2>_c = Var(O).   [exact]
  nu = 1/2 d_1 + 1/2 d_4 : M0=1  Var=1  chi=5/8  w1=1/2
  nu = 3/4 d_2 + 1/4 d_4 : M0=1  Var=1  chi=7/16  w1=3/4
  nu = 1/5 d_9 + 4/5 d_4 : M0=1  Var=1  chi=2/9  w1=1/5
 => 'divide by M0' and 'divide by Var(O)' are THE SAME functional (same carrier, same channel).

