==============================================================================
[8] STRUCTURAL: no absolute threshold is carrier-invariant
==============================================================================
 given any family with f1^2(L) > 0, put s_L := sqrt(r0/(2 f1^2(L))); then (s_L^2 f1^2) = r0/2 < r0
 and (2^0.5 s_L) gives 2 r0 > r0 : the predicate flips inside the admissible group {O -> s O, s>0}.
   L=  8: s_L=2.267249e-01 -> s^2 f1^2=0.250000 (<r0) ; 1.41421*s_L -> 0.500000 (>r0)
   L= 16: s_L=1.133625e-01 -> s^2 f1^2=0.250000 (<r0) ; 1.41421*s_L -> 0.500000 (>r0)
 => ill-definedness is STRUCTURAL, not a property of the free-field family.

